{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-sya2-jtlo-n6uv-pmpi","published":"2026-11-11T18:18:24Z","modified":"2026-11-16T02:36:15.987686950Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-18728"],"summary":"A flaw was found in open-iscsi. An integer underflow vulnerability in the `iscsiuio` component, specifically during…","details":"A flaw was found in open-iscsi. An integer underflow vulnerability in the `iscsiuio` component, specifically during IPv4 Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP) parsing, allows a remote attacker on the same local network segment to cause a denial of service. By sending a specially crafted IPv4/UDP DHCP reply, the attacker can trigger an out-of-bounds read, leading to the `iscsiuio` process crashing. This issue affects systems where `iscsiuio` is actively handling IPv4 DHCP traffic.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"open-iscsi","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/open-iscsi"},"versions":["2.1.10-r4","2.1.12-r0","2.1.12-r1"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-sya2-jtlo-n6uv-pmpi.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://scout.docker.com/v/DHI-sya2-jtlo-n6uv-pmpi"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-18728"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2463029"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-18728"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://security.alpinelinux.org/vuln/CVE-2026-18728"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://alas.aws.amazon.com/AL2/ALAS-2026-3897.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-18728"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-18727"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-18726"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-18725"},{"type":"ADVISORY","u